WEBVTT

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.650
I'm losing strength.

00:00:05.650 --> 00:00:09.860
Goddesses inside an Anti-Crystal field will continue to lose their strength and energy.

00:00:10.910 --> 00:00:13.610
Who are you?

00:00:13.610 --> 00:00:16.100
My name is Arfoire.

00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:18.710
I'll be the one to bring joyous tidings of chaos

00:00:18.710 --> 00:00:21.800
to this world ruled by you four young ladies.

00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:25.240
And I'm Pirachu.

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:28.300
The third-most popular mascot in mouse society.

00:00:28.300 --> 00:00:29.680
Mouse...

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:32.410
Don't steal my spotlight!

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:33.630
Listen to yourself.

00:00:34.070 --> 00:00:40.390
<i>I</i> was the one who dug up the Anti-Crystals from the Lastation caves and the Leanbox seafloor.

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:46.480
And it was <i>my</i> discovery of the first crystal in a Planeptune forest that set everything in motion.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:50.900
Not to mention, did I not carry out the unenviable task of stealing one from Lowee's Basilicom?

00:00:51.380 --> 00:00:53.400
Lowee's Basilicom?

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:56.470
Blanc, did you know about that rock...

00:00:56.470 --> 00:00:58.210
Yeah, I did.

00:00:58.210 --> 00:01:00.060
I had it under tighter security than Fort Knox,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.660
but after the kidnapping incident, it was nowhere to be found.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.920
If you'd just told us about it...

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:10.690
How was I meant to know there were so many of 'em?

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:12.670
The caves?

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:16.440
Don't tell me...

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:17.960
What's wrong, Noire?!

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:21.510
Zoinks!

00:01:22.550 --> 00:01:23.580
My transformation...

00:01:28.240 --> 00:01:29.800
I believe I told you

00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.320
that as long as you stayed in that field,

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.500
you'd continue to lose your strength and energy.

00:01:40.140 --> 00:01:41.700
How could this be?

00:01:43.230 --> 00:01:44.450
Sis...

00:01:45.710 --> 00:01:48.020
Sis!

00:01:49.730 --> 00:01:50.920
Nepgear?

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:53.520
Get back on, Nepgear.

00:01:53.520 --> 00:01:54.630
But Sis...

00:01:56.230 --> 00:01:56.970
Nepgear!

00:02:01.980 --> 00:02:03.260
Right now, we have to get out of here!

00:02:06.530 --> 00:02:08.230
That one's getting away.

00:02:08.230 --> 00:02:09.400
It matters not.

00:02:09.740 --> 00:02:13.510
She's a mere CPU Candidate who can't even transform yet.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:02.260
What's this all about, IF?

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:04.840
I'm not exactly sure,

00:04:04.840 --> 00:04:07.040
but they mentioned an "anti-crystal" or something.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.340
That's probably what's sealing the goddesses' powers.

00:04:11.340 --> 00:04:12.860
"Anti-Crystal"?

00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.770
Could you look into it for us, Histoire?

00:04:15.770 --> 00:04:19.280
Certainly, but it'll take me three days.

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:22.490
As soon as possible, please.

00:04:22.940 --> 00:04:24.100
I'll see what I can do.

00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:27.930
Anyway, Nepgear and the gang should return to Planeptune.

00:04:27.930 --> 00:04:31.500
I believe it'd be better for Uni and the others to go back home too.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.030
Good bye.

00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:37.740
Well, you heard her—

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.090
Hang on!

00:04:39.360 --> 00:04:42.560
Do you seriously expect us to just go home because she says so?

00:04:42.560 --> 00:04:44.460
Give us a proper explanation!

00:04:44.460 --> 00:04:48.100
Usually, Sis would knock baddies out in one blow!

00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:51.310
Is Sis gonna die?

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:53.680
I-I'm sure she'll be fine.

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:57.140
Goddesses don't go down that easily—

00:04:57.140 --> 00:04:58.150
But...

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:00.960
I heard something about "sealing their powers" earlier.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:02.080
I'm sorry.

00:05:05.980 --> 00:05:07.560
It's not your fault, Ge-Ge.

00:05:07.560 --> 00:05:08.570
No.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.940
That rock I picked up back when we went shopping...

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:17.790
Surely that had to be an Anti-Crystal.

00:05:18.880 --> 00:05:19.970
Let's not do this.

00:05:19.970 --> 00:05:21.820
Hindsight is 20/20.

00:05:21.820 --> 00:05:22.900
Why?

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:28.460
If only I'd thought more carefully about why I felt dizzy back then...

00:05:29.070 --> 00:05:32.170
If only I'd told Sis and the others about it...

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.060
You idiot!

00:05:34.330 --> 00:05:39.760
My sister is really, really strong,

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.910
but because of you, she's...

00:05:42.900 --> 00:05:45.900
<i>You</i> should've taken her place instead!

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.550
Aww, jeez.

00:06:11.550 --> 00:06:12.890
I'm bored outta my skull!

00:06:12.890 --> 00:06:14.560
I wanna play some games!

00:06:14.560 --> 00:06:17.210
What is <i>wrong</i> with you?

00:06:17.210 --> 00:06:19.470
We're captives, you know.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:23.960
But I wish I could at least use Four Goddesses Online's chat system.

00:06:23.960 --> 00:06:27.070
I'm supposed to be meeting my fellow guild members.

00:06:27.340 --> 00:06:28.480
Not you too.

00:06:28.480 --> 00:06:31.860
Well, it's good to see you're still the same as ever.

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:32.840
Okay!

00:06:32.840 --> 00:06:34.700
Let's go out on a limb and make some demands!

00:06:35.180 --> 00:06:37.340
Hey!

00:06:37.340 --> 00:06:39.870
I know you're there!

00:06:39.870 --> 00:06:41.710
Bar Whore!

00:06:41.710 --> 00:06:43.710
Who're you calling a bar whore?!

00:06:43.710 --> 00:06:45.210
Uh...

00:06:45.210 --> 00:06:47.100
CFW Magic?

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:48.760
That's someone else entirely!

00:06:48.760 --> 00:06:50.750
Okay then, Arfaemon!

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:53.670
Gimme something to kill some time with.

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:55.470
I'm gonna die of boredom otherwise!

00:06:56.330 --> 00:07:00.730
Either way, your lives are headed toward their end.

00:07:00.730 --> 00:07:01.630
Huh?

00:07:01.630 --> 00:07:03.310
She didn't object to that one.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:05.890
Can I just call her Arfaemon from now on?

00:07:05.890 --> 00:07:07.230
I don't care!

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:09.040
Hey, you listenin' to me?!

00:07:09.040 --> 00:07:12.230
Someone's sentencing you to death here, you know.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:13.490
What? Come again?

00:07:14.530 --> 00:07:16.240
Take a look beneath you.

00:07:17.410 --> 00:07:18.290
Zoinks!

00:07:19.410 --> 00:07:20.410
What the hell is this?

00:07:20.960 --> 00:07:22.550
It's creepy.

00:07:22.550 --> 00:07:25.060
Is this another effect of the Anti-Crystals?

00:07:38.100 --> 00:07:45.090
Soon, you will begin to suffer, and eventually, you will die.

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:52.570
Enjoy what little time you have left.

00:08:04.690 --> 00:08:05.940
Nepgear.

00:08:05.940 --> 00:08:06.990
Come on!

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:08.550
I know.

00:08:14.750 --> 00:08:16.080
Uni.

00:08:17.160 --> 00:08:19.240
Let's make up.

00:08:27.500 --> 00:08:29.950
I went too far.

00:08:31.370 --> 00:08:32.630
I'm sorry.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:37.990
Don't be.

00:08:38.310 --> 00:08:39.650
I know.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:42.030
I know!

00:08:43.370 --> 00:08:45.430
It's not your fault,

00:08:46.510 --> 00:08:48.170
I know!

00:08:51.390 --> 00:08:52.140
Yeah.

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.010
And I know how you feel.

00:09:17.290 --> 00:09:21.790
I thought there couldn't be anyone stronger than my sister.

00:09:22.350 --> 00:09:27.110
That everything would be fine as long as she was around.

00:09:27.730 --> 00:09:28.920
I'm the same.

00:09:28.920 --> 00:09:32.590
I can't do anything without my sister either.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.260
Even now, I have no idea what to do—

00:09:36.260 --> 00:09:38.050
It's simple!

00:09:38.670 --> 00:09:40.550
We just need to rescue them!

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:45.980
I want to save them too.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:49.770
But we can't transform...

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:51.770
Then we just need to change that!

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:53.980
Let's learn how to do it.

00:09:54.320 --> 00:09:57.240
Can we?

00:09:57.750 --> 00:09:59.630
Sis said something about how

00:10:00.710 --> 00:10:06.750
I can't transform because I'm
subconsciously limiting myself.

00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:09.990
Limiting myself...

00:10:11.260 --> 00:10:15.760
Like, the things we're scared about are holding us back.

00:10:16.490 --> 00:10:18.910
I'm scared of monsters.

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:20.870
Yup, me too.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:25.060
Then let's train until we're not scared of them anymore!

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:27.980
Sounds good!

00:10:30.190 --> 00:10:31.180
Yeah.

00:10:34.810 --> 00:10:36.130
Uni?

00:10:36.130 --> 00:10:37.900
Rom! Ram!

00:10:38.600 --> 00:10:40.010
Your ride's here—

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:49.900
Owwie.

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.290
This hurts quite a lot!

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.790
You okay, Compa?

00:10:54.140 --> 00:10:55.570
I'm perfectly fine!

00:10:55.570 --> 00:10:57.100
This is training!

00:10:57.100 --> 00:10:57.870
Huh?

00:10:58.630 --> 00:11:01.270
This is Vert's game, isn't it?

00:11:01.270 --> 00:11:03.700
We figured we'd get some combat training done.

00:11:03.700 --> 00:11:06.560
Remember how she said there was a combat simulation mode?

00:11:07.040 --> 00:11:10.290
I took on the role of the enemy.

00:11:10.290 --> 00:11:15.060
If this can help Ge-Ge and the gang transform, I'll be super glad!

00:11:15.060 --> 00:11:16.320
Transform?

00:11:16.870 --> 00:11:21.580
We all decided to go save our sisters!

00:11:21.580 --> 00:11:24.330
That's why we want to get stronger.

00:11:24.330 --> 00:11:26.260
Hold on, Nepgear.

00:11:26.260 --> 00:11:28.830
We're up against someone who already captured the goddesses!

00:11:29.250 --> 00:11:32.850
Even so, I believe we have to do this.

00:11:33.320 --> 00:11:36.840
We've inherited the goddesses' power, too.

00:11:40.250 --> 00:11:41.840
I had a feeling this would happen.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.850
But you're not a good foil, Compa.

00:11:47.850 --> 00:11:49.250
I'll do it.

00:11:49.250 --> 00:11:50.330
Iffy.

00:11:51.120 --> 00:11:52.400
Relax. It's fine.

00:11:52.400 --> 00:11:53.690
Let's do this.

00:11:56.270 --> 00:11:57.190
Found you!

00:12:00.640 --> 00:12:01.270
Huh?

00:12:06.150 --> 00:12:06.950
Hey!

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:09.380
Aren't you done uploading the pictures yet?

00:12:09.380 --> 00:12:12.630
Never in my wildest dreams did I imagine I'd have to use an analog connection.

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:16.360
Not to mention, the modem we found in the trash was a 56k one.

00:12:16.360 --> 00:12:17.630
I'm about to cry here.

00:12:17.630 --> 00:12:20.920
You were fully aware there was no cellphone reception in this area!

00:12:21.480 --> 00:12:24.300
Mistakes made in the field are an employer's responsibility.

00:12:25.490 --> 00:12:26.760
Anyway, get on with it.

00:12:28.260 --> 00:12:31.050
Tell the <i>modem</i> to get on with it.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.210
Oh?

00:12:33.210 --> 00:12:35.110
I see it's just the Candidates here.

00:12:35.110 --> 00:12:37.520
None of the CPUs are around, huh?

00:12:37.880 --> 00:12:39.750
I <i>knew</i> it! Something went down, didn't it?

00:12:39.750 --> 00:12:40.800
Uh...

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:43.150
If I'm not mistaken, you're Abnes, right?

00:12:43.150 --> 00:12:45.190
Hey, we're busy!

00:12:45.190 --> 00:12:46.280
Do not disturb!

00:12:46.580 --> 00:12:47.800
Who's she?

00:12:47.800 --> 00:12:51.860
The little girl lover who they say got Neppy mad back at Lowee.

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.680
Abnes...

00:12:54.070 --> 00:12:55.250
We don't really have time right now—

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:57.040
Shaddup!

00:12:58.110 --> 00:13:01.680
Ex-little girls who've grown all half-assed are trash!

00:13:02.360 --> 00:13:03.790
Now that the goddesses aren't around,

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:07.540
this is my chance to let Rom and Ram go back to being normal little girls.

00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:09.410
Nice idea, even if I do say so myself.

00:13:09.410 --> 00:13:11.560
Or should I say, "a flash of inspiration"?

00:13:12.030 --> 00:13:14.000
Come now, little girls.

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.680
Let us hold hands and play!

00:13:18.730 --> 00:13:21.680
Um, we don't wanna hold hands.

00:13:21.680 --> 00:13:23.190
We wanna play that instead.

00:13:24.270 --> 00:13:25.200
That?

00:13:26.430 --> 00:13:27.240
Please!

00:13:28.550 --> 00:13:30.330
Well, if you insist.

00:13:34.940 --> 00:13:37.050
S-Say, little girl.

00:13:37.050 --> 00:13:38.960
Are you really okay with this?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:41.340
Why don't we play something a little more girly?

00:13:42.840 --> 00:13:45.090
Charge, girls!

00:13:45.090 --> 00:13:46.330
Take that!

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:47.460
Hold on a second!

00:13:47.460 --> 00:13:47.980
Iffy, apparently you can fight AI characters too.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.290
Wait!

00:13:49.290 --> 00:13:51.530
All right, let's do this!

00:13:51.530 --> 00:13:52.740
I knew it.

00:13:52.740 --> 00:13:53.530
I'm sorry!

00:13:53.530 --> 00:13:55.080
Nearly every game has that mode.

00:13:57.910 --> 00:13:59.610
Wanna tell them about it?

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:00.970
I'm sorry!

00:14:00.970 --> 00:14:01.770
Why don't we...
I'm sorry!

00:14:01.770 --> 00:14:02.560
Why don't we...

00:14:02.560 --> 00:14:03.860
save it for later?

00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:06.860
They look like they're having fun.

00:14:09.680 --> 00:14:11.130
Never give up...

00:14:11.130 --> 00:14:13.740
on little girls!

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:23.380
This is the end!

00:14:34.140 --> 00:14:35.770
Wow!

00:14:36.270 --> 00:14:39.400
They gave that Ancient Dragon a good beating!

00:14:39.400 --> 00:14:40.020
Ow!

00:14:40.020 --> 00:14:41.980
That hurts, you quack nurse!

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:43.770
I'm sorry.

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.320
We killed quite a lot of monsters,

00:14:46.320 --> 00:14:48.900
but it's not helping us transform.

00:14:48.900 --> 00:14:50.110
Yep.

00:14:50.110 --> 00:14:52.660
But if we kill a lot more...

00:14:52.660 --> 00:14:54.740
Looks like we don't have time for that anymore.

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:02.040
News of the four goddesses' capture will soon spread like wildfire.

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:04.250
The goddesses got captured?!

00:15:04.250 --> 00:15:06.090
That leaves the little girls wide open—

00:15:06.800 --> 00:15:09.630
You need some rest!

00:15:11.800 --> 00:15:14.300
If the public saw these pictures,

00:15:14.300 --> 00:15:17.100
it might lead to a Share crash.

00:15:17.100 --> 00:15:18.600
And if that happens...

00:15:19.020 --> 00:15:23.770
...we'll receive less power from the Share Crystals.

00:15:23.770 --> 00:15:27.530
That means we need to save our sisters before this gets in the way!

00:15:34.620 --> 00:15:35.450
Yep.

00:15:39.200 --> 00:15:41.040
It's accumulated quite a lot.

00:15:41.040 --> 00:15:44.210
What'll happen to us when we get swallowed by that?

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:48.010
I should've looked into some counter-measures.

00:15:48.010 --> 00:15:50.420
But I only thought about keeping it as far from me as possible.

00:15:50.420 --> 00:15:52.590
Chin up, gals!

00:15:53.220 --> 00:15:55.050
We're fine right now,

00:15:55.050 --> 00:15:57.100
and there's still hope for us!

00:15:57.100 --> 00:15:59.600
I don't usually mind your optimism,

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:01.810
but it gets really annoying at times like these.

00:16:01.810 --> 00:16:03.350
You're trying to escape from reality.

00:16:03.350 --> 00:16:06.610
I'm just saying, it's better than thinking we're doomed.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:10.070
False hope never did anyone any good.

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.820
I don't think it's false hope at all.

00:16:11.820 --> 00:16:12.610
You what?
Huh?

00:16:13.070 --> 00:16:16.870
Have you forgotten about your sisters?

00:16:18.990 --> 00:16:20.410
Uni?

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.870
She's never even fought without me by her side.

00:16:24.250 --> 00:16:28.500
Rom and Ram are still at an age where I have to keep them safe, too.

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.050
Nepgear seems level-headed, but she's quite spoiled.

00:16:32.050 --> 00:16:33.930
I think it'd be too much for her.

00:16:33.930 --> 00:16:37.890
Isn't that just your ego at play?

00:16:40.560 --> 00:16:43.600
Sure, they're extremely lovely girls.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:49.070
I'd love for them to forever stay the way they are too.

00:16:51.860 --> 00:16:55.950
But those thoughts might be

00:16:55.950 --> 00:17:00.120
what's letting them stay as "precious little sisters who can't transform".

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:02.790
Do you not feel that way?

00:17:07.080 --> 00:17:08.040
They're here.

00:17:08.880 --> 00:17:13.170
As expected, the CPU Candidate came back with friends.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.050
Hmph.

00:17:14.050 --> 00:17:16.390
What can they do?

00:17:16.720 --> 00:17:19.760
They probably can't even reach this place.

00:17:19.760 --> 00:17:21.640
Don't you agree?

00:17:28.770 --> 00:17:32.530
They still can't transform, yet...

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.190
It doesn't matter if the goddesses fail.

00:17:34.190 --> 00:17:37.280
People will come to terms with it if their sisters give it their all.

00:17:37.280 --> 00:17:40.620
That'll reduce the damage done to the Shares.

00:17:40.910 --> 00:17:42.490
You're right, but...

00:17:43.000 --> 00:17:44.370
Also,

00:17:44.960 --> 00:17:46.670
I want to believe in them too.

00:17:47.170 --> 00:17:49.130
I want to believe they can do it.

00:17:49.460 --> 00:17:50.630
Iffy...

00:17:51.340 --> 00:17:52.920
Ready, girls?

00:18:14.230 --> 00:18:15.990
You'd best prepare yourselves!

00:18:20.820 --> 00:18:23.330
I'll keep you safe, Ram!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:24.370
Okay!

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:26.330
And I'll take care of the rest!

00:18:37.590 --> 00:18:38.430
Hit!

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:43.930
Pain, pain, fly away!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:45.680
Outta my way!

00:19:00.450 --> 00:19:01.740
Nepgear!

00:19:02.240 --> 00:19:03.240
Ram!

00:19:04.240 --> 00:19:05.240
Rom!

00:19:11.000 --> 00:19:12.040
Rom! Ram!

00:19:12.040 --> 00:19:13.250
Regroup!

00:19:13.790 --> 00:19:15.090
Uni...

00:19:15.090 --> 00:19:15.750
Behind you!

00:19:25.100 --> 00:19:26.180
I refuse to lose!

00:19:42.280 --> 00:19:43.370
Get away!

00:19:43.370 --> 00:19:44.570
Stay away from me!

00:19:47.700 --> 00:19:48.790
<i>What have I done?</i>

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:50.960
<i>I was mistaken.</i>

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:53.750
<i>It was too early for us to go into battle!</i>

00:19:53.750 --> 00:19:54.540
Iffy, they're all gonna be killed!

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.210
<i>Everyone will die because of me!</i>

00:19:56.210 --> 00:19:57.500
I know!

00:19:59.720 --> 00:20:02.010
<i>I can't do a thing!</i>

00:20:02.010 --> 00:20:04.340
<i>Help me, Sis!</i>

00:20:06.100 --> 00:20:08.220
<i>I'm relying on Sis again.</i>

00:20:09.310 --> 00:20:11.060
<i>But I...</i>

00:20:11.060 --> 00:20:13.560
<i>really do need Sis by my side!</i>

00:20:13.560 --> 00:20:15.560
Sis said something about how

00:20:15.560 --> 00:20:22.490
I can't transform because I'm
subconsciously limiting myself.

00:20:22.490 --> 00:20:23.660
Limiting...

00:20:24.110 --> 00:20:27.200
Like, the things we're scared about are holding us back.

00:20:27.660 --> 00:20:30.620
<i>What I'm scared about is...</i>

00:20:30.620 --> 00:20:32.540
<i>losing Sis.</i>

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:36.380
<i>No longer being Sis's kid sister.</i>

00:20:36.790 --> 00:20:38.750
<i>No, that's not it.</i>

00:20:40.420 --> 00:20:44.220
<i>I'm scared of becoming stronger than her!</i>

00:20:46.260 --> 00:20:47.260
Iffy!

00:20:47.260 --> 00:20:48.510
Look at Ge-Ge!

00:20:52.480 --> 00:20:57.520
<i>I wanted to keep looking up to her forever,</i>

00:20:57.520 --> 00:21:01.400
<i>but if this is what it takes to bring her back...</i>

00:21:01.990 --> 00:21:05.530
I'll become stronger than anyone else in the world!

00:21:27.640 --> 00:21:28.970
Nepgear!

00:21:32.720 --> 00:21:34.310
Nepgear.

00:21:36.350 --> 00:21:37.770
Amazing!

00:21:43.940 --> 00:21:46.150
I cannot retreat here.

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:47.570
So...

00:21:50.410 --> 00:21:52.540
I gotta do this!

00:23:25.590 --> 00:23:27.090
Looks like we don't have time for that anymore.

00:23:27.090 --> 00:23:28.010
Huh?

00:23:32.260 --> 00:23:33.760
No, wait, this doesn't count!

00:23:33.760 --> 00:23:34.930
Let's have a do-over!

00:23:34.930 --> 00:23:37.810
It's just, Compa sort of happened to say I could stay over,

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:40.100
and I wouldn't have taken this except I woke up at midnight and—
